Maybe you are not even strong enough to carry the partially eaten
corpse.  I received a letter from another net-hacker that asked why they
would be able to lift the corpse at all to eat it.  And I said that it
was probably simulating the idea that the character had to sit down to
eat the corpse and when he was attacked he stood back up, (Which is
simulated by dropping the corpse).  Now, you could have it so you could
#sit to eat a corpse on the ground, and have the game say something
like, "You can not attack while sitting down." but I am not sure it is
nessecary, because it IS possible to lift something you can't carry long
enough to eat it.  The way I see it, carrying implies that you can move
around with it, eating a corpse on the ground, doesn't require the
ability to move about with it.  If you really want to get picky, you
could also point out that the character would have to unwield his weapon
in order to eat the food.  It all depends how realistic you want to get
with the food code.  I am of the opinion that the current code is fine. 
If the game designers and my fellow net-hackers want to change it in
order to make it more realistic, I would have to say
	A) Make getting hungry a rare thing, food could also be rare.  
	B) I would agree with the water camp, that water is much more nessecary
than food, and realistically, harder to get in a dungeon.

anyways, those are my thoughts on the subject
